s.add(0), state[0] as u64);\n251\t    store_bigendian_32(statebytes.add(4), state[1] as u64);\n252\t    store_bigendian_32(statebytes.add(8), state[2] as u64);\n253\t    store_bigendian_32(statebytes.add(12), state[3] as u64);\n254\t    store_bigendian_32(statebytes.add(16), state[4] as u64);\n255\t    store_bigendian_32(statebytes.add(20), state[5] as u64);\n256\t    store_bigendian_32(statebytes.add(24), state[6] as u64);\n257\t    store_bigendian_32(statebytes.add(28), state[7] as u64);\n258\t\n259\t    inlen\n260\t}\n261\t\n262\t/// `crypto_hashblocks_sha512`: absorbs `inlen / 128` full blocks, returns the\n263\t/// number of unprocessed trailing bytes.\n264\tunsafe fn crypto_hashblocks_sha512(\n265\t    statebytes: *mut u8,\n266\t    mut inp: *const u8,\n267\t    mut inlen: u64,\n268\t) -> u64 {\n269\t    let mut state = [0u64; 8];\n270\t\n271\t    let mut a = load_bigendian_64(statebytes.add(0));\n272\t    state[0] = a;\n273\t    let mut b = load_bigendian_64(statebytes.add(8));\n274\t    state[1] = b;\n275\t    let mut c = load_bigendian_64(statebytes.add(16));\n276\t    state[2] = c;\n277\t    let mut d = load_bigendian_64(statebytes.add(24));\n278\t    state[3] = d;\n279\t    let mut e = load_bigendian_64(statebytes.add(32));\n280\t    state[4] = e;\n281\t    let mut f = load_bigendian_64(statebytes.add(40));\n282\t    state[5] = f;\n283\t    let mut g = load_bigendian_64(statebytes.add(48));\n284\t    state[6] = g;\n285\t    let mut h = load_bigendian_64(statebytes.add(56));\n286\t    state[7] = h;\n287\t\n288\t    while inlen >= 128 {\n289\t        let mut w = [0u64; 80];\n290\t        for i in 0..16 {\n291\t            w[i] = load_bigendian_64(inp.add(8 * i));\n292\t        }\n293\t        for i in 16..80 {\n294\t            w[i] = small_sigma1_64(w[i - 2])\n295\t                .wrapping_add(w[i - 7])\n296\t                .wrapping_add(small_sigma0_64(w[i - 15]))\n297\t                .wrapping_add(w[i - 16]);\n298\t        }\n299\t\n300\t        for i