{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_3vic2alzpvqkr6ojux46eha7yixfc6htschx75tepel3l7rbgaiq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass across all 48 feature combinations.\n\n## What was done\n\n**Phase A — surface mapping** (3 artifacts, all derived mechanically from the C):\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — all 60 C-exported symbols (union of `libblake.so`, `libsphincs_core_det.so`, `libsphincs_core.so`) plus a per-backend table and a source-file coverage table proving all 27 C files were translated.\n- `ERRORS.md` — 57 rows, one per distinct rejection/no-check path found by grepping every `return -1`, `return RNG_*`, `== NULL`, range check and `#error`.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 53 rows over the cross-product of build axes (4 backends × 2 thash × 6 secpar), runtime input shapes, and **all** public entry points including the lowest-level ones (`SPX_treehash` with its FFI function pointer, `SPX_wots_gen_leafx1`, `blake*_compress`, `sha*_inc_blocks`, `haraka_S_inc_*`, `cst`).\n\n**Phases B/C — differential tests** (`tests/differential.rs`, 3000 lines, 102 tests): both C and Rust are loaded via `libloading` and called only through `dlsym`. Two design hazards were handled — the test binary deliberately does not link the crate, and the Rust `.so` is loaded **first** with `RTLD_NOW|RTLD_LOCAL` so the C libraries can never bind to it. Three negative controls confirm the harness actually detects divergence (wrong thash → 41 failures; wrong secpar/backend → immediate assert).\n\n**Phase D** — `symdiff.sh` (0 missing symbols × 48), `check_all.sh` (49 configs clean), `run_all.sh` (48 × 102 tests), `kat_all.sh` (C driver digest == Rust driver digest == `expected_kat.txt`, 48/48).\n\n## Bugs fixed in the Rust (the C was never touched)\n\n3 missing exports (`AES256_ECB`, `DRBG_ctx`, `cst` — the last two were *behavioural* gaps, not just naming: the DRBG's observable global state was hidden behind a private `Mutex`), the `spx_ctx` size mismatch for `sha2-128s/f` (144 vs C's 72), and 3 wrapping-arithmetic sites (`seedexpander`'s `16 - buffer_pos` underflow, `bytes_to_ull`'s ≥64-bit shift, `compute_root`'s `tree_height - 1`).\n\n## Notable finding\n\n`lib/blake/src/hash_blake.c` passes **byte** counts to `blake*_update`, which takes **bits** — so for the BLAKE parameter sets only ~1/8 of the message reaches the digest and `crypto_sign_verify` accepts a modified message tail. I confirmed this with a standalone C-only program against the reference `.so`s, verified the Rust reproduces it byte-for-byte, and corrected my *test expectation* rather than the code. Documented in `ERRORS.md`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1166,"cache_read_input_tokens":441572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1166,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0a57186a-e772-4c86-931a-f38c37ec34b0","uuid":"58202aa6-4e4c-42f1-b176-e8d771243d0f","timestamp":"2026-08-21T15:58:49.702Z"}
